ic parashat empire also  known as the imperium at the head of  this empire is emperor shadom iv who  administers contracts allowing various  houses of the lands rod to extract spice  from the planet the landsrod is the body  that represents all the great houses of  the imperium among the landsrod two  powerful houses have emerged the noble  house atreides ruled by duke lado and  the malevolent house harkonnen ruled by  vladimir harkinan they rule from their  respective planets of caledon and gidi  prime so while the emperor is supposed  to maintain the peace so that the spice  can flow there are two other entities  with tremendous power that seek to  maintain stability these are the  benedescerate and the spacing guild the  spacing guild is run by the guild  navigator this weird ass creature who is  actually a human who has mutated due to  massive amounts of exposure to spice  melange the navigator can transport  these ships called highliners throughout  space in a process known as space  folding without the space guild space  travel at faster than light speeds would  not be possible so you can see how much  power these guys wield and this power  wouldn't be possible without the spice  the last important organization i want  to cover in this video is the bene  jesserit an all-female group of  quasi-religious scientific spies and  nuns who use their powers to guide  humanity along a path of insight and  stability their powers include that  appreciance the ability to see the past  present and future and if that wasn't  enough the reverend mothers the highest  rank in the bene jesuit can even untap  an ability called other memory allowing  them to access memories lost to time for  90 generations the beneficiary have  carried out a system of selective  breeding with an attempt to bring  stability to the universe they plan to  breed the daughter of duke lado atreides  with a harkonnen male which would bring  the end to the centuries-old feud  between these two houses think of it  like alliances through marriage in  medieval times but lady jessica a  benedescerate tasked with producing a  female with duke lado atreides disobeyed  her orders after falling in love with  him and instead bore him a son paul the  bender gestured have the ability to  choose the sex of their offspring and  this totally threw off the plans of the  reverend mother gaius helen moyim who  believed lady jessica's female heir  would go on to give birth to the quisats  hararak a type of prophetic figure who  would bring stability to the universe  who could also see into the future and  this is where the events of the dune  film really start lady jessica's  decision to have a male have thwarted  years of benedescerate planning and now  the benedescerate need to find a new way  to bring stability to the universe  ensuring that this spice will flow at  the beginning of dune the emperor benne  jester at space guild and harkinan all  conspire to destroy house atreides in an  attempt to bring stability the emperor  justifies his actions by telling the  guild navigator that he is fearful of  both the rising popularity of duke  atreides among the landsrod and their  development of a new weapon which  utilizes sound so the emperor along with  the harkonnen devise a sneak attack to  wipe out house atreides on arrakis and  establish hearken and dominance on the  desert planet the events that follow are  mainly told from the perspective of paul  atreides our film's protagonist and son  of duke lato it is hinted that he may be  the one spoken about in the prophecy  that kwitsat's hattarak he has dreams of  the future and when tested by the  reverend mother she exclaims no woman  child ever withstood that much if he is  indeed the one she may be able to  control him could he be the one  maybe  but will he be ours to control  upon arriving on arrakis we learn of a  group of indigenous inhabitants known as  the fremen it's actually their prophecy  that depicts this kwitsat hararak a male  the son of abena jesurite who would lead  them to freedom after house atreides is  betrayed in an attack that sees duke  lado killed paul escapes into the desert  with his mother this is where the real  test to see if he is the one begins he  teams up with a group of friend and  fighters who initially agreed to take  him in an exchange for teaching them the  weirding way advanced fighting  techniques of the benedescerate that  allows fighters teleport teleport-like  abilities mainly used in hand-to-hand  combat this was replaced in the film  version with these devices called  weirding modules they aren't in the do  novel and david lynch added them because  he didn't like the idea of quote kung fu  on sand dunes in the film but for paul  to fully transform into this prophetic  figure he must first drink from the  water of life a poisonous blue liquid  that was used by the benedictura to turn  their sisters into reverent mothers only  those with powerful control over their  mind and body can withstand the poison  and until paul any man who tried to  drink it had died paul ends up surviving  the process and it gives him enormous  powers he can see into the future and  how the emperor deceived him he'll also  have the ability to control the  sandworms and ability used in the film's  final act this gives him the title  moadib a freman word for their religious  and political leader now i personally  didn't like the end battle known as the  battle of era keen portrayed in the 1984  version where the fremen led by paul  boadib defeat the emperor and the  harkonnens part of this was that it was  terribly one-sided paul and the freeman  basically show up with a [ __ ] ton of  sand worms and weirding modules and  completely wiped the floor with their  enemies this meant there was little  tension in the film's final act an act  which should have the most but this  ending is all part of paul's  well-orchestrated plan while he's  fighting alongside the fremen he sent  